hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16162","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, he heard Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi say: The people of Sham are the whip of Allah in the earth; He avenges with them of whom He wills how He wills. And unlawful for their hypocrites to overcome their believers. And they will die only in grief or anger or sorrow."
"16163","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said: Tayyaf al-Iskandarani narrated to us, from Ibn Sharahil ibn Bukayl, from his father Shurahbil, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I have kin in Egypt who take of these grapes. He said: And did any of the Muslims do that? I said: Yes. He said: Do not be as the Jews: fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and ate their prices. He said: I said: What say you of a man who took a bunch, squeezed it, and drank it? He said: No harm. When I descended he said: What is lawful to drink is lawful to sell."
"16164","He said: Haytham narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maymun al-Ashari narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, raised it. He said: Whatever tree shades over a people, its owner has the choice of cutting what shaded or eating its fruit."
"16165","He said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad, meaning Ibn al-Munkadir, narrated to me, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing in the market on the day of Eid, looking, while the people pass."
"16166","He said: Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, and Yazid said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said ibn Khalid, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman, he said: A physician mentioned medicine at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and mentioned the frog that is in medicine, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing it."
"16167","He said: Surayj and Harun narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the lost property of the pilgrim. And Harun said in his hadith: Amr ibn al-Harith. Abdullah said: And I heard it from Harun."
